sbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, KAZUHIDE</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ICHIHASHI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA KAZUHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ICHIHASHI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, KAZUHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing adipic acid which comprises using an element of the platinum group and oxidizing hydroxycaproic acid and/or  epsilon -caprolactam with oxygen or an oxygen-containing gas. Use of this method makes it unnecessary to use nitric acid resulting in the formation of nitrogen oxide as a by-product or employing considerably high pressure.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de production d'acide adipique, le procédé consistant à prendre un élément du groupe des platines et à oxyder de l'acide hydroxycaproïque et/ou  epsilon -caprolactame avec de l'oxygène ou un gaz contenant de l'oxygène. Ce procédé rend inutile l'utilisation d'acide nitrique, ce qui entraîne la formation d'oxyde d'azote comme produit dérivé, ou l'utilisation d'une pression très élevée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>